!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/a-composed-constructor-is-applied-as-its-parent-is-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.3, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.6, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.8, [TSON-SCHEMA] §8.1"
  description: """
    `my_list => meta.array & { min_items?: = 1 }` is a constructor, IS-A `meta.array` by composition, so it has the
    argument slot `meta.array` has: `element_type`, its one required field typed by a reference naming types and
    pinned by nothing. `my_list<text>` is `!my_list { element_type: text }`, the construction of `my_list` and not of
    `meta.array`, and is written so: the binding record headed by the applied constructor, holding the field the
    application bound. `min_items` is pinned in `my_list`'s own declaration, so it comes from the vocabulary and is not
    in the binding record. At a field's type the same application is that construction written in place.
    """
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        tags => !my_list { element_type: text }
        page => !meta.record {
          fields: { labels => !meta.record_field { type: { of: !my_list { element_type: text } } } }
        }
      }
      """
  }
}
